            <div xml:id="d36">

                <pb facs="0112" n="22" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg22"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/931</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Harbin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Moser</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-01-10"><hi rendition="#italic">January 10, 1918</hi></date>.
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 3.23 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Reliable telegram dated 9th states Irkutsk quiet under Bolshevik control. Consuls
                    active protecting foreigners and have refused deliver to Bolsheviks high
                    provisional officials who took refuge in Chinese Consulate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moser</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
